docs {
  ## Delete Spaces File (Superuser)

  Permanently deletes one file from DigitalOcean Spaces. **Superuser role
  only** — any other authenticated role gets `403`. There is no trash/undo —
  this is a real delete against the live Space.

  Use `objectKey` exactly as returned by `GET /uploads/spaces-files` (the
  `files[].objectKey` field), URL-encoded in the query string.

  Deleting an object here does **not** remove any reference to its URL that
  may already be saved on an expense/visit/task-activity/etc. row in our own
  database — that row would be left pointing at a now-missing file. Confirm
  the file isn't still referenced before deleting.

  ### Query params

  | Field     | Type   | Required | Notes                                                    |
  |-----------|--------|----------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
  | objectKey | string | yes      | must start with the configured Spaces folder (e.g. `MyActivity/`) — a key outside it is rejected with `400` |

  ### Response — `data` object

  | Field     | Type   | Notes                     |
  |-----------|--------|---------------------------|
  | objectKey | string | the key that was deleted  |
}
